{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanChiPerRep","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanChiPerRep","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Rat","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform_unit_laurent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform_unit_laurent","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L184-L191","doc":"The published Borromean q-rational character instantiated over the\nnon-field `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`: it is the Laurent polynomial `chi21_borromean` at\n`h = T − T⁻¹`.  Concrete witness of `chi21_borromean_qform_unit_eq_poly`\nover a commutative ring that is not a field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.TUnit","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L180-L182","doc":"`T` is a unit of `ℤ[q, q⁻¹] = LaurentPolynomial ℤ`, with inverse `T(-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_hform_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_hform_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L160-L168","doc":"The h-form is purely even in `h = q − q⁻¹` (bar-invariant under\n`q ↦ q⁻¹`): replacing `q` by `q⁻¹` sends `h ↦ −h` and the even powers\n`h⁴, h⁶` are unchanged. Stated directly as invariance under `q ↦ 1/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_hform_eq_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_hform_eq_poly","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L152-L158","doc":"The `ℚ` h-form is exactly the `R[h]` polynomial character\n`chi21_borromean` evaluated at `h = q − q⁻¹`.  Connects the archimedean\nh-form to the faithful `R[h]` object above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform_eq_hform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform_eq_hform","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L144-L150","doc":"**The two published forms of `χ^{(2,1)}(β_Bor)` are equal** for every\nnon-zero `q` in any field. Pure field identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_hform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_hform","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L139-L142","doc":"The standard-irrep Borromean character in its h-polynomial form,\n`2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶` with `h = q − q⁻¹` (written `q − 1/q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L135-L137","doc":"The standard-irrep Borromean character in its q-rational form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform_unit_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform_unit_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L114-L120","doc":"Bar-invariance over units: `q ↦ q⁻¹` fixes the character, since it sends\n`h = ↑q − ↑q⁻¹ ↦ −h` and `chi21_borromean` is even.  Division-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform_unit_eq_poly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform_unit_eq_poly","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L93-L112","doc":"**The published q-rational form equals the faithful `R[h]` character.**\n`chi21_borromean_qform_unit q = chi21_borromean (↑q − ↑q⁻¹)` over any\ncommutative ring with `q` a unit — division-free, the sole hypothesis is\n`↑q · ↑q⁻¹ = 1`.  Hence the Borromean standard-irrep character is a genuine\n`ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` Laurent polynomial, not merely a rational function over a field.\n(The `linear_combination` coefficient is the exact quotient of\n`qform − chi21_borromean(↑q−↑q⁻¹)` by `↑q·↑q⁻¹ − 1`, machine-derived; the\nresidual is closed by `ring`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_qform_unit","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L87-L91","doc":"The published q-rational Borromean character `(−q¹² + ⋯ − 1)/q⁶`, over a\ncommutative ring with `q` a unit: division by `q⁶` is `(↑q⁻¹)⁶`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean_even","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L59-L64","doc":"The `R[h]` character `2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶` is even in `h` (bar-invariant under\n`h ↦ −h`, i.e. `q ↦ q⁻¹`): only even powers `h⁴, h⁶` appear. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi21_borromean","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanChiPerRep.lean#L54-L57","doc":"The standard-irrep Borromean character as a polynomial in `h`:\n`χ^{(2,1)}(β_Bor) = 2 − 3h⁴ − h⁶`.  This is the faithful `R[h]` form\n(no division); `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}